+// Fix 173c: on 1.0.6-work-fix173b the same GTA IV session (15951112 bytes loaded, 15951112 in the
+// snapshot, no new pipeline) was written again and timed out: the driver serializes its pipeline
+// cache in another order each time, so the bytes differ though the content does not. A snapshot of
+// the size on the drive is also not written when no pipeline was made this session since the file
+// was last noted (the cache counts the pipelines it creates outside the start's stored ones); a new
+// pipeline adds an entry and the size grows, so either rule alone would not do. A write cut off by
